thread:
rhea: Quick bug from onboarding sample-app. We noticed rerank scores were wrong for a small subset of docs. Repro: batch of 3, one item retried, final vectors paired by position end up misaligned.

omar: Which helper + sdk? Node? Rust?

rhea: Node helper (embed-util v1.1). Behavior: it sends chunks concurrently, and if a single item is retried the helper appends the single response when it arrives. If that arrives before another chunk finishes we get a scrambled order. Example timeline: send [a,b] and [c]; b times out, retry b solo; responses arrive: [a,b-from-chunk], b-retry, c. Helper push => [a,b,b,c]? (we had duplicated positions because server returned position-only arrays and helper merged naively).

jin: Duplication plus mis-ordering is worse. Sounds like the helper both concatenates and doesn't dedupe by id. Two fast fixes: 1) preserve index mapping and place results into preallocated array slots; 2) attach a transient request id or original index in the outbound envelope so merging can match items.

omar: Also raise an idempotency header on retries so server can dedupe if it supports that behavior. This prevents duplicate vectors if a retry hits after the original landed.

rhea: Current minimal helper snippet (simplified):

```js
async function embedMany(items){
  const chunks = chunk(items, 2);
  const out = [];
  await Promise.all(chunks.map(async c => {
    try{
      const r = await client.embeddings.create({input:c.map(i=>i.text)});
      out.push(...r.data);
    }catch(e){
      for(const it of c){
        const rr = await client.embeddings.create({input:[it.text]});
        out.push(rr.data[0]);
      }
    }
  }));
  return out; // fragile
}
```

jin: Proposed patch: preallocate results = new Array(items.length), record mapping of item -> idx before send, and on any response place vectors into results[idx]. Also, when retrying attach a small header `x-idempotency-key: <item-guid>` and expose a feature flag `echo_items:true` so server can return [{id, embedding}] if callers opt-in.

omar: Good. Add unit tests that randomize response delays and assert final ordering equals input order and no duplicates. Also test the duplicate-dedup behavior when idempotency header is honored by the server.

rhea: I'll PR the helper change and update sample-app README to state: "helpers guarantee input-order; do not depend on server ordering unless you set echo_items".

ci-bot: ci/test-embed-util: added index-preserve + idempotency tests (simulated network races) - triggered by @rhea branch.

jin: After Node PR, let's do a Rust and Python parity pass. Python currently returns tuples with ids in our infra tests but double-check.

omar: Agreed. Thanks for the clear repro and small patch plan. This would've been a subtle production issue for rerank-heavy customers. :thumbsup:
